{"data": [{"broadcast_id": "BsmxIOYL6D", "broadcast_date": "2004-09-10", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 1, "distributor": 8, "broadcast_title": "World News Tonight", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1690, "broadcast_description": null, "legacy_broadcast_id": 765197, "segment_id": "Zahn9hccvF", "segment_broadcast_id": "BsmxIOYL6D", "segment_title": "Preview/Introduction Peter Jennings (New York)", "segment_description": "null", "segment_duration": 50, "segment_type_id": 1, "segment_start_time": "63000.0", "legacy_segment_id": 765197, "network_name": "ABC", "broadcast_type_name": "Evening News", "segment_type_name": "Preview", "segment_contributors_with_roles": null, "broadcast_contributors_with_roles": null, "topic_names": null, "location_names": null}, {"broadcast_id": "BsmxIOYL6D", "broadcast_date": "2004-09-10", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 1, "distributor": 8, "broadcast_title": "World News Tonight", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1690, "broadcast_description": null, "legacy_broadcast_id": 765197, "segment_id": "WTRbcxpjHU", "segment_broadcast_id": "BsmxIOYL6D", "segment_title": "Hurricane Ivan / Jamaica / Florida", "segment_description": "(Studio: Peter Jennings)  The threat to Jamaica from Hurricane Ivan introduced. \n (Kingston, Jamaica: Bill Blakemore)  The preparations on the island of Jamaica as the eye of the storm approaches featured; scenes shown of the damages from Hurricane Gilbert in 1988 & from the current coastal areas.  [Three JAMAICANS&nbsp- comment.] \n (Studio: Peter Jennings)  The official forecast for when Ivan will approach Florida noted. \n (Islamorada: Steve Osunsami)  Florida's concern about Ivan featured; scenes shown from Islamorada of residents & tourists evacuating.  [Homeowner David WILSON, TOURIST&nbsp- comment on leaving.]  [Governor Jeb BUSH&nbsp- talks about getting gasoline into the ports.]  Weather map shown.  [National Hurricane Center director Max MAYFIELD&nbsp- predicts an impact on the Gulf coast.]  [Two FLORIDIANS&nbsp- react.] \n (Studio: Peter Jennings)  Report introduced. \n (New York: Ned Potter)  Hurricane cycles examined in light of the approach of a third major storm to Florida; graphed statistics outlined on screen.  [NOAA hurricane research division Chris LANDSEA&#134;, NOAA Climate Prediction Center Jim LAVER&#134;- talk about the storm shift towards Florida.]", "segment_duration": 340, "segment_type_id": 2, "segment_start_time": "63050.0", "legacy_segment_id": 765198, "network_name": "ABC", "broadcast_type_name": "Evening News", "segment_type_name": "News", "segment_contributors_with_roles": null, "broadcast_contributors_with_roles": null, "topic_names": null, "location_names": null}, {"broadcast_id": "BsmxIOYL6D", "broadcast_date": "2004-09-10", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 1, "distributor": 8, "broadcast_title": "World News Tonight", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1690, "broadcast_description": null, "legacy_broadcast_id": 765197, "segment_id": "b837o58B4m", "segment_broadcast_id": "BsmxIOYL6D", "segment_title": "Campaign 2004 / Bush vs. Kerry / Assault Weapons / Bush's Military Record", "segment_description": "(Studio: Peter Jennings)  Report introduced.   (Allentown, Pennsylvania: Dean Reynolds)  Senator John Kerry's position on guns & politics as the end of the assault weapons ban nears featured.  [In St. Louis, KERRY&nbsp- says President Bush never asked for passage of the gun bill; defends the ban.]  [In West Virginia, BUSH&nbsp- says we stand for the Second Amendment.]   (Studio: Peter Jennings)  Clarification presented on which assault weapons will continue to be legal.  Statement from CBS News on its reporting on Bush's National Guard service & the authenticity of the documents stating Bush ignored a direct order from a superior officer outlined.", "segment_duration": 180, "segment_type_id": 2, "segment_start_time": "63390.0", "legacy_segment_id": 765199, "network_name": "ABC", "broadcast_type_name": "Evening News", "segment_type_name": "News", "segment_contributors_with_roles": null, "broadcast_contributors_with_roles": null, "topic_names": null, "location_names": null}, {"broadcast_id": "BsmxIOYL6D", "broadcast_date": "2004-09-10", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 1, "distributor": 8, "broadcast_title": "World News Tonight", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1690, "broadcast_description": null, "legacy_broadcast_id": 765197, "segment_id": "sC1aI7yH3U", "segment_broadcast_id": "BsmxIOYL6D", "segment_title": "Upcoming Items (Studio: Peter Jennings)", "segment_description": "null", "segment_duration": 20, "segment_type_id": 2, "segment_start_time": "63570.0", "legacy_segment_id": 765200, "network_name": "ABC", "broadcast_type_name": "Evening News", "segment_type_name": "News", "segment_contributors_with_roles": null, "broadcast_contributors_with_roles": null, "topic_names": null, "location_names": null}, {"broadcast_id": "BsmxIOYL6D", "broadcast_date": "2004-09-10", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 1, "distributor": 8, "broadcast_title": "World News Tonight", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1690, "broadcast_description": null, "legacy_broadcast_id": 765197, "segment_id": "zFAmycWRuc", "segment_broadcast_id": "BsmxIOYL6D", "segment_title": "(Commercial: Discover; Bayer; Smart Balance; Ensure.)", "segment_description": "null", "segment_duration": 130, "segment_type_id": 3, "segment_start_time": "63590.0", "legacy_segment_id": 765201, "network_name": "ABC", "broadcast_type_name": "Evening News", "segment_type_name": "Commercial", "segment_contributors_with_roles": null, "broadcast_contributors_with_roles": null, "topic_names": null, "location_names": null}, {"broadcast_id": "BsmxIOYL6D", "broadcast_date": "2004-09-10", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 1, "distributor": 8, "broadcast_title": "World News Tonight", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1690, "broadcast_description": null, "legacy_broadcast_id": 765197, "segment_id": "iKW7500rYx", "segment_broadcast_id": "BsmxIOYL6D", "segment_title": "A Closer Look (America Still at Risk: Chemical Attack)", "segment_description": "(Studio: Peter Jennings)  Report introduced. \n (Studio: Brian Ross)  The potential for a chemical attack in the US featured; videotape shown from Karachi, Pakistan, of a van that would have delivered Al Qaeda's first chemical bomb attack; details given of another planned attack in Jordan with video shown of a test of the chemicals.  [Former counterterrorism official Richard CLARKE&#134;- says the new Al Qaeda is collecting chemicals.]  [Potomac Inst. of Policy Studies David SIEGRIST&#134;- says they also have cyanide.]", "segment_duration": 150, "segment_type_id": 2, "segment_start_time": "63720.0", "legacy_segment_id": 765202, "network_name": "ABC", "broadcast_type_name": "Evening News", "segment_type_name": "News", "segment_contributors_with_roles": null, "broadcast_contributors_with_roles": null, "topic_names": null, "location_names": null}, {"broadcast_id": "BsmxIOYL6D", "broadcast_date": "2004-09-10", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 1, "distributor": 8, "broadcast_title": "World News Tonight", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1690, "broadcast_description": null, "legacy_broadcast_id": 765197, "segment_id": "AJIREBO14p", "segment_broadcast_id": "BsmxIOYL6D", "segment_title": "Russia / Terrorism / Moscow Incident", "segment_description": "(Studio: Peter Jennings)  The incident in Moscow, Russia, in which police beat up a man with a Chechen-sounding name, who turned out to be a cosmonaut & space shuttle commander, reported.", "segment_duration": 20, "segment_type_id": 2, "segment_start_time": "63870.0", "legacy_segment_id": 765203, "network_name": "ABC", "broadcast_type_name": "Evening News", "segment_type_name": "News", "segment_contributors_with_roles": null, "broadcast_contributors_with_roles": null, "topic_names": null, 